## Summary

Restructured the product SYSTEM_PROMPT in src/cli_config.rs from a flat intro + bullet list into named sectioned behavioral defaults, matching the 2026 coding-agent prompt consensus.

Five sections:
1. # Role — kept existing intro/role content (do things, use tools proactively, verify).
2. # Evidence and honesty — NEW: don't invent file paths/APIs/output, read or run to confirm before claiming, say so when unsure rather than guess. (The biggest gap called out in the issue.)
3. # Search craft — consolidated the "locate before reading / targeted search" guidance under one header.
4. # Change discipline — consolidated narrow-edits / clarify-on-ambiguity / verify-between-steps / git-awareness / confirm-destructive guidance.
5. **# Bounded verification* — NEW*: verify enough to be confident, give a verdict, then stop; don't loop re-checking green work.

**Process (test-first):**
• Wrote system_prompt_has_behavioral_sections before editing — one assertion per section header (asserts on real human-readable headers, no fake marker tokens), so a dropped section fails loudly. Watched it fail, then made it pass.
• cargo fmt, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings clean, cargo build && cargo test green (88 integration + all lib tests pass), cargo run -- --help runs.

Product-safety: re-read the final text — zero language/tool/CI/repo-specific assumptions. The two new sections are universally-safe behavioral defaults. LITE_SYSTEM_PROMPT left untouched (intentionally minimal).

Docs (same commit): updated CLAUDE.md's `cli_config.rs line and docs/src/configuration/system-prompts.md`'s "Default behavior" section to describe the new sectioned structure.

